; ENUM (RFC 6116) in network B. Its own numbers, +1 202 555 0151 and
; 0152, lead to the SIP URIs of those numbers in its own domain, which
; are the public identities of its subscribers; network A's numbers lead
; to global numbers in SIP URIs of network A's domain with user=phone
; (TS 29.165 8.1), which the S-CSCF of network B sends to IBCF-B. All
; are fictional numbers of the North American Numbering Plan.
$ORIGIN e164.arpa.
$TTL 60
@  IN SOA dns.ims.mnc002.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org. hostmaster.ims.mnc002.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org. 1 3600 600 86400 60
@  IN NS  dns.ims.mnc002.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org.

; +1 202 555 0151 and 0152, the UEs of network B.
1.5.1.0.5.5.5.2.0.2.1 IN NAPTR 10 100 "u" "E2U+sip" "!^.*$!sip:+12025550151@ims.mnc002.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org!" .
2.5.1.0.5.5.5.2.0.2.1 IN NAPTR 10 100 "u" "E2U+sip" "!^.*$!sip:+12025550152@ims.mnc002.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org!" .

; +1 202 555 0101 and 0102, the UEs of network A.
1.0.1.0.5.5.5.2.0.2.1 IN NAPTR 10 100 "u" "E2U+sip" "!^.*$!sip:+12025550101@ims.mnc001.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org;user=phone!" .
2.0.1.0.5.5.5.2.0.2.1 IN NAPTR 10 100 "u" "E2U+sip" "!^.*$!sip:+12025550102@ims.mnc001.mcc001.3gppnetwork.org;user=phone!" .
